<h2 id="scribe-v2" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Scribe v2</h2>
<p>Scribe v2 is our state-of-the-art speech recognition model designed for accurate transcription across 90+ languages. It provides precise word-level timestamps and advanced features like speaker diarization and dynamic audio tagging.</p>
<p>This model excels in scenarios requiring accurate speech-to-text conversion:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Transcription Services</strong>: Perfect for converting audio/video content to text</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Meeting Documentation</strong>: Ideal for capturing and documenting conversations</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Content Analysis</strong>: Well-suited for audio content processing and analysis</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Multilingual Recognition</strong>: Supports accurate transcription across 90+ languages</li>
</ul>
<p>Key features:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class="">Accurate transcription with word-level timestamps</li>
<li class="">Speaker diarization for multi-speaker audio</li>
<li class="">Dynamic audio tagging for enhanced context</li>
<li class="">Support for 90+ languages</li>
<li class="">Entity detection</li>
<li class="">Keyterm prompting</li>
<li class="">Transcript editing</li>
</ul>
<p>Read more about Scribe v2 <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/overview/capabilities/speech-to-text">here</a>.</p>
<h2 id="scribe-v2-realtime" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Scribe v2 Realtime</h2>
<p>Scribe v2 Realtime, our fastest and most accurate live speech recognition model, delivers state-of-the-art accuracy in over 90 languages with a median time to committed transcript of ~150ms. See <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/eleven-api/concepts/latency-methodology">how latency is measured</a>.</p>
<p>This model excels in conversational use cases:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Live meeting transcription</strong>: Perfect for realtime transcription</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">AI Agents</strong>: Ideal for live conversations</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Multilingual Recognition</strong>: Supports accurate transcription across 90+ languages with automatic language recognition</li>
</ul>
<p>Key features:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class="">Ultra-low latency: Get committed transcripts with a median latency of ~150 milliseconds</li>
<li class="">Streaming support: Send audio in chunks while receiving transcripts in real-time</li>
<li class="">Multiple audio formats: Support for PCM (8kHz to 48kHz) and μ-law encoding</li>
<li class="">Voice Activity Detection (VAD): Automatic speech segmentation based on silence detection</li>
<li class="">Manual commit control: Full control over when to finalize transcript segments</li>
<li class="">Entity detection</li>
<li class="">Entity redaction</li>
<li class="">Transcript editing</li>
</ul>
<p>Read more about Scribe v2 Realtime <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/overview/capabilities/speech-to-text">here</a>.</p>
<h2 id="scribe-v2-medical" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Scribe v2 Medical</h2>
<p>Scribe v2 Medical is a batch speech recognition model specialized for medical and clinical audio. It is a fine-tune of Scribe v2 that improves recognition of drug names, anatomy, pathology, and clinical dictation while matching Scribe v2’s accuracy on everyday speech. It uses the same Speech to Text API as Scribe v2 and is billed at the same rate. Pass <code>scribe_v2_medical</code> as <code>model_id</code>.</p>
<div data-intent="note" class="fern-callout"><div class="flex items-start space-x-4"><div class="[&amp;_svg]:size-icon-md mt-0.5 w-4"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-pin"><path d="M12 17v5"></path><path d="M9 10.76a2 2 0 0 1-1.11 1.79l-1.78.9A2 2 0 0 0 5 15.24V16a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-.76a2 2 0 0 0-1.11-1.79l-1.78-.9A2 2 0 0 1 15 10.76V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1 2 2 0 0 0 0-4H8a2 2 0 0 0 0 4 1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"></path></svg></div><div class="-my-4 flex-1 overflow-x-auto text-sm before:mb-4 before:block after:mt-4 after:block"><div class="font-heading text-base font-semibold leading-snug"></div><h3 id="intended-purpose" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Intended purpose</h3><p>Scribe v2 Medical is a batch Speech-to-Text API model for developers and
organizations to integrate into applications that convert clinical audio, including
clinician-patient conversations, dictation, intake and care-coordination calls, into draft
transcripts for documentation and related administrative workflows. The resulting text is intended
for review and correction by a healthcare professional or other authorized user before use. Scribe
v2 Medical is not intended to interpret clinical information or provide diagnoses, treatment
recommendations, clinical decisions or other clinical guidance.</p></div></div></div>
<p>This model is well-suited for:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Clinical documentation</strong>: Ambient encounters and notes where medical terms surface mid-conversation</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Dictation</strong>: Dense sequences of medications, dosages, and findings</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Intake and coordination calls</strong>: Patients describing their own conditions, often over the phone</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Compliance workflows</strong>: Combine with <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/eleven-api/guides/how-to/speech-to-text/batch/entity-detection">entity detection</a> for PHI categories</li>
</ul>
<p>Key features:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class="">Same request shape as Scribe v2 (<code>keyterms</code>, <code>entity_detection</code>, <code>no_verbatim</code>, diarization, timestamps)</li>
<li class="">Improved recognition of medication names, anatomy, and pathology terms</li>
<li class="">No regression on everyday speech versus Scribe v2</li>
<li class="">Support for 90+ languages</li>
<li class="">Speaker diarization for multi-speaker audio</li>
<li class="">Dynamic audio tagging</li>
<li class="">Entity detection, including PHI categories</li>
</ul>
<p>Scribe v2 Medical is a batch model. For live transcription, use Scribe v2 Realtime.</p>
<p>Scribe v2 Medical is eligible for HIPAA, with Business Associate Agreements available to Enterprise customers as well as Zero Retention Mode (ZRM). With ZRM enabled, audio input and text output are deleted immediately after each request completes. ElevenLabs retains nothing, and your application receives the full API response and retains transcripts under your own controls.</p>
<div data-intent="info" class="fern-callout"><div class="flex items-start space-x-4"><div class="[&amp;_svg]:size-icon-md mt-0.5 w-4"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-info"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4"></path><path d="M12 8h.01"></path></svg></div><div class="-my-4 flex-1 overflow-x-auto text-sm before:mb-4 before:block after:mt-4 after:block"><div class="font-heading text-base font-semibold leading-snug"></div><p>Companies requiring HIPAA compliance must contact <a class="fern-mdx-link" href="https://elevenlabs.io/contact-sales">ElevenLabs
Sales</a> to sign a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) before
sending protected health information.</p></div></div></div>
<p>Read more about Speech to Text <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/overview/capabilities/speech-to-text">here</a>.</p>
<h2 id="sfx-v3" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">SFX v3</h2>
<p>SFX v3 (<code>eleven_text_to_sound_v3</code>) is our newest sound effects model. It uses the same <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/api-reference/text-to-sound-effects/convert">Sound Effects API</a> as <code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2</code>: set <code>model_id</code> to <code>eleven_text_to_sound_v3</code> to use it. <code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2</code> is still the default but is deprecated and will be removed on March 1, 2027.</p>
<p>Compared with <code>eleven_text_to_sound_v2</code>, SFX v3:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class="">Follows several instructions in one prompt, such as “Football crowd cheering, hearing a ball drop, crowd booing”.</li>
<li class="">Handles prompts that include music or vocals, such as “Gospel choir singing hello”.</li>
<li class="">Produces more natural-sounding results.</li>
<li class="">Is less likely to clip on high-frequency sounds such as gongs, chimes and whistles.</li>
</ul>
<p>Results vary by prompt, so compare both models on your own prompts before switching.</p>
<p>SFX v3 supports looping. Set <code>loop</code> to <code>true</code> to generate a sound effect that loops smoothly.</p>
<p>In ElevenCreative, SFX v3 is available in Sound Effects, Flows and Studio.</p>
<p>Read more about sound effects <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/overview/capabilities/sound-effects">here</a>.</p>
<h2 id="eleven-realtime" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Eleven Realtime</h2>
<p>Eleven Realtime is a new class of Speech to Speech models for building natural voice agents. Each Realtime model is a complete voice agent: speech recognition, voice activity detection and turn-taking, LLM, and text to speech, selected and tuned by ElevenLabs to work together as one system. Select a Realtime model and you get a well-performing agent from a single choice, with no components to configure.</p>
<p>Two Realtime models are available.</p>
<p><strong class="font-semibold">Eleven Realtime v1 Mini</strong> is optimized for fast, natural conversation and works well in the following scenarios:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">AI assistants</strong>: Fast, expressive dialogue where the conversation itself is the product.</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Educational tutors</strong>: Natural back-and-forth that keeps up with the learner’s pace.</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Interactive characters</strong>: Expressive characters for games and entertainment.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong class="font-semibold">Eleven Realtime v1 Max</strong> is optimized for complex tasks and works well in the following scenarios:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Customer support</strong>: Resolving queries that require following a process and looking up information.</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Lead qualification</strong>: Structured conversations that gather information and decide next steps.</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Multi-step workflows</strong>: Tasks that call tools to look things up or take actions.</li>
</ul>
<p>Key features:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--grayscale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:content-[&#x27;⦁&#x27;] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class="">Speech recognition, turn-taking, language model, and voice in one model choice</li>
<li class="">Natural turn-taking and interruption handling</li>
<li class="">Tool calling</li>
<li class="">Customizable voices from the ElevenLabs voice library</li>
<li class="">Support for 90+ languages</li>
<li class="">Switch between v1 Mini and v1 Max with a model selection, not an integration change</li>
</ul>
<p>Eleven Realtime is available in ElevenAgents, where you select a Realtime model from the model dropdown, and via the Realtime API, which is designed to be compatible with OpenAI’s Realtime API over WebSocket. If you are already using OpenAI’s Realtime API, see the <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/eleven-agents/guides/openai-realtime-compatibility">migration guide</a>.</p>
<h3 id="supported-languages-4" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Supported languages</h3>
<p>Realtime models support 90+ languages. See the <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/overview/models#supported-languages">Eleven v4 language list</a>.</p>
<p>Read more about Eleven Realtime <a data-astro-prefetch="viewport" class="fern-mdx-link" href="/docs/eleven-agents/customization/realtime-models">here</a>.</p>
<h2 id="eleven-music" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Eleven Music</h2>
<p>Eleven Music is our studio-grade music generation model. It allows you to generate music with natural language prompts in any style.</p>
<p>This model is excellent for the following scenarios:</p>
