<h2 id="concurrency-and-priority" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Concurrency and priority</h2>
<p>Your subscription plan determines how many requests can be processed simultaneously and the priority level of your requests in the queue.
Speech to Text has an elevated concurrency limit.
Once the concurrency limit is met, subsequent requests are processed in a queue alongside lower-priority requests.
In practice this typically only adds ~50ms of latency.</p>
